The matching Cython code has more levels:

```cython
cdef inline double log1pexp(double x) noexcept nogil:
    if x <= -37:
        return exp(x)
    elif x <= -2:
        return log1p(exp(x))
    elif x <= 18:
        return log(1. + exp(x))
    elif x <= 33.3:
        return x + exp(-x)
    else:
        return x
```

I think reflecting this in the array api version could further align the numerical stability of both branches and might make it possible to make the logistic regression compliance test pass with lower tolerance levels without scaling the data for all `float32` cases.

