review_comment:
`test_kineto` is intended to be accelerator-agnostic, but it currently contains logic that specifically depends on CUDA and ROCm:

```Python
found_gemm = False
        found_memcpy = False
        found_mm = False
        for e in p.function_events:
            if "aten::mm" in e.name:
                found_mm = True
            if "gemm" in e.name.lower() or "Cijk" in e.name:
                found_gemm = True
            if "memcpy" in e.name.lower() or "__amd_rocclr_copyBuffer" in e.name:
                found_memcpy = True
        if use_cuda:
            self.assertTrue(found_gemm)
            self.assertTrue(found_memcpy)
        else:
            self.assertTrue(found_mm)
```

Therefore, I suggest moving these test cases into a separate class and using a decorator to restrict their execution to CPU and CUDA only in next PR and leave the deeper refactor for future update.

