review_comment:
Thanks for flagging! Actually self_cuda_time_total is deprecated in favor of self_device_time_total -  see [torch/autograd/profiler_util.py lines 968-973](https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/blob/main/torch/autograd/profiler_util.py#L968-L973):

```
@deprecated(
    "`self_cuda_time_total` is deprecated. Use `self_device_time_total` instead.",
    category=FutureWarning,
)
def self_cuda_time_total(self):
    return self.self_device_time_total

```
The table() sort logic (line 1241) also normalizes "cuda" → "device" internally, so both keys resolve to the same attribute. Using self_device_time_total aligns with the device-agnostic direction, let me know thoughts!

