review_comment:
actually one way to do this better is we can define a function in the model prepare_inputs_for_export which pre-computes the dynamic tensors, wdyt ? should be useful for compilation as well so the name is misleading.
```python
# in modeling_qwen2_vl.py
class Qwen2VLForConditionalGeneration(...):
    def prepare_inputs_for_export(self, inputs):
        if "grid_thw" in inputs:
            inputs["cu_seqlens"] = get_vision_cu_seqlens(inputs["grid_thw"])
            inputs["position_ids"] = get_vision_position_ids(inputs["grid_thw"], self.spatial_merge_size)
        return inputs
```

In a way the more centralized all patches / fixes are the better? 
You tell me if it makes sense or not, I am fine with ths, but also: 
```python 
MAPPING = {
    "minicpmv4_6_vision" : { "onnx": {"forward" : [...], "attributes": [...], "patches"}}
     "qwen_vl": {}
}
```
